course: dictionary
lesson: 7695
title: Old words with a grand sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are old. You will meet them in old books, and people today sometimes use them as a joke. Provender is one of these words. It means food, but it is old-fashioned, so you will rarely hear it in everyday talk.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, the animals talk about good provender for a trip. The context tells you it is something you pack and take along, like food. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Food fits, so provender means food.
explain: Provender has two uses. For horses and farm animals, it means dry food such as hay and oats. For people, it is a humorous word for food. Today you might say, «Bring plenty of provender for the picnic!» to make your family laugh.
fact: Provender means food.
fact: In its old meaning, provender is dry food for horses and farm animals, such as hay and oats.
fact: When used as a joke, provender means food for people.
fact: Provender is uncountable, so you say some provender, not a provender.
fact: Provender is an old-fashioned word, so it sounds grand and a little funny.
exercise: «Bring plenty of provender for the picnic!» What does provender mean here? | A picnic blanket | *Food | Rain clouds | Plates and cups
exercise: Dad says, «Bring plenty of provender for the picnic!» Is he being serious about the food? | No, he means it will rain | Yes, he wants you to find a horse | *No, he is joking, using an old word for food | Yes, he means the picnic is cancelled
exercise: Which phrase is correct? | two provender | *some provender | a provender | provenders
test: For a farm horse, what is provender? | Water from a stream | *Dry food such as hay and oats | Sweets and cakes | Fresh grass from the lawn
test: Which word means about the same as provender? | Across | At once | Noise | *Food
exam: Which sentence uses provender correctly? | Provender means a long, cold winter. | The provender was loud and sudden. | *The farmer filled the bin with provender for the horses. | She ran provender across the field.
